# Embroidery Inventory Manager

## Stack
- Node/Express `server.js`, MongoDB Atlas, static `index.html` / `styles.css` / `script.js`
- Local: **http://localhost:3002** (`.env` `PORT=3002`). Never use `file://`.
- Live: Vercel (`embroidery-inventory-manager.vercel.app`)

## Data
- Authenticated **GET/POST `/api/snapshot`** is the primary path (inventory, customers, sales, invoices).
- Legacy `/api/inventory` etc. require session; prefer snapshot for load/save.
- Credentials only in `.env` / Vercel env — not in code.

## Shop commission (business rule)
- **10%** for shop consignment (Flippin' Happy / First Avenue / shop-vendor customers).
- Node source: `lib/shop-commission.js`. Browser mirror: `SHOP_VENDOR_AUTO_COMMISSION_PERCENT` in `script.js`.
- Keep email automation and UI in sync; run `npm run test:commission`.

## Agent workflow
- **Do not git commit or push** unless the user explicitly asks in that message.
- Prefer small, focused diffs; match existing style in `script.js`.
- After server/route changes: user must restart `node server.js`.
- Verify with `npm run test:smoke` when touching UI (needs local server + `.env`).
- Human context: see `agent.md`. Historical audits: `audit/website-2026-10-27/` (some items superseded).